<title>THAILAND: Merrill says no need yet to be alarmed on baht.</title>
<headline>Merrill says no need yet to be alarmed on baht.</headline>
<dateline>BANGKOK 1997-07-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>U.S. investment bank Merrill Lynch still overweights Thailand despite jitters over the embattled baht, it said on Monday in a new report.</p>
<p>However, it noted that optimism for the Thai market could be adversely affected if the baht were to remain stuck in the 31.00-33.00 baht per dollar range for a sustained period of time.</p>
<p>&quot;A sustained period of time means more than one month. That has not been the case yet,&quot; said a Merrill Lynch analyst.</p>
</text>
